    "targetFormat": "BGRA8_UNORM, RGBA8_UNORM, A2B10G10R10_UNORM or A2R10G10B10_UNORM; the attachment format owns channel packing and no manual swizzle is performed",
    "presentationDepth": "a 10:10:10:2 display image keeps its codes on a 10-bit target; on an 8-bit target modes.w bit 0 is set and each tap shows the top 8 bits of its code",
    "sourceAlpha": "straight; channel remap applied per texel tap, then premultiplied before the bilinear weights",
    "overlayAlpha": "premultiplied; composited last",
    "channelEnum": "matches bloom::ui::ViewerChannel (Rgba,Rgb,Red,Green,Blue,Alpha)",
    "backdrop": "surroundColor outside the destination rectangle; inside it frameColor (the composition background), or the checkerboard when modes.y (transparency grid) is set; every backdrop colour is display-encoded and opaque",
    "checkerboard": "inside the destination rectangle only, and only with the transparency grid on; raised tiles where (row+column) is even, tile pixels and origin supplied by the caller"
